// Title: Capsh Shell Invocation - Linux
// Sigma ID: db1ac3be-f606-4e3a-89e0-9607cbe6b98a
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Li Ling, Andy Parkidomo, Robert Rakowski, Blake Hartstein (Bloomberg L.P.)
// Date: 2024-09-02 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution, T1059
// Description: Detects the use of the "capsh" utility to invoke a shell.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://gtfobins.github.io/gtfobins/capsh/#shell
//   - https://www.elastic.co/guide/en/security/current/linux-restricted-shell-breakout-via-linux-binary-s.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/linux/process_creation/proc_creation_lnx_capsh_shell_invocation.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "/capsh" and ProcessCommandLine endswith " --"
